      <room>AW1.124</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Mapping Wikileaks&#39; Cablegate using Python, mongoDB, Neo4J and Gephi</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Data Analytics devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Text analysis and graph visualization on the Wikileaks Cablegate dataset.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We propose to present a complete work-flow of textual data analysis, from acquisition to visual exploration of a complex network. Through the presentation of a simple software specifically developed for this talk, we will cover a set of productive and widely used softwares and libraries in text analysis, then introduce some features of Gephi, an open-source network visualization &amp;amp; analysis software, using the data collected and transformed with cablegate-semnet.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1871">Elias Showk</person>
          <person id="1872">Julian Bilcke</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>